<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n17283" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">ex-sūgo</span></b>  (<b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">exūg-</span></b> ), xi, ctum, 3
		(anteclass. forms of second conj., <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b><i>imper.</i> exsugeto,
				<i><span class="en">Cato, R. R. 156, 3</span></i>; <i>fut.</i> exsugebo, <i><span class="en">Plaut. Ep.
				2, 2, 5</span></i>), v. a., <i>to suck
			out</i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">umorem,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Varr. R. R. 2, 4, 15</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">liquorem de materia,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Vitr.
					2, 8, 2</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">sanguinem alicui (alicujus),</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Plaut. Poen. 3, 2, 37</span></i>
			; <i><span class="en">id. Ep. 2, 2, 5</span></i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">vulnus,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Cels.
					5, 27, 3</span></i>
			; cf. 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">venena,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Plin.
					23, 1, 27, § 57</span></i>
			. —Hence, <b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">exsuctus</span></b>  (<b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">exuct-</span></b> ), a, um, P. a., <i>sucked out</i>, <i>dried up</i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">segetes exsuctiores,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Varr. R. R. 2, 7, 11</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">infirmum corpus et exsuctum,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Sen. Ep. 30, 1</span></i>
			.</div>
